      '**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-27 21:53 UTC\n\n**Story 1: Monorepo root config and Docker** \u2014 completed by devops_engineer\n\n**DEC-001: Monorepo structure established**\n- Created root `package.json` with workspace configuration for `backend/`, `frontend/`, `mobile/`\n- Docker multi-stage build: Node 20 alpine base, backend compile stage, frontend Vite build stage, production stage with nginx\n- `docker-compose.yml` with PostgreSQL 16 + Redis for local development\n- `bin/dev` startup script with process management for backend (tsx watch), frontend (vite), and database health check\n- `.gitignore` covers node_modules, dist, .env, coverage across all workspaces\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-27 22:01 UTC\n\n**Story 2: Backend Express scaffolding** \u2014 completed by backend_developer\n\n**DEC-001: Backend architecture established with Express + TypeORM**\n\nCreated the core backend structure following enterprise patterns:\n\n1. **Express app** (`backend/src/index.ts`): CORS, helmet, compression, JSON body parser, request logging with Winston\n2. **TypeORM connection** (`backend/src/shared/db/connection.ts`): PostgreSQL with SSL support, migration auto-run, connection pooling (max 20)\n3. **Health endpoint** (`backend/src/api/health.ts`): Returns `{ status: "ok", timestamp, version, uptime }` with database connectivity check\n4. **Auth middleware stub** (`backend/src/shared/auth/`): JWT verification against Cognito JWKS endpoint, extracts `userId` and `orgId` from claims\n5. **Error handling**: Global error handler with structured JSON responses, request ID tracking via `x-request-id` header\n6. **TypeScript config**: Strict mode, ES2022 target, path aliases (`@shared/*`, `@api/*`)\n\nThe backend compiles cleanly with `tsc --noEmit` and starts on port 3001 with `tsx watch`.\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-28 17:41 UTC\n\n**Story 3: React frontend with auth shell** \u2014 completed by frontend_developer\n\n**DEC-001: Frontend scaffolded with React 19 + Vite + TailwindCSS**\n\nImplemented the complete frontend shell:\n\n1. **App shell** with React Router v7: public routes (landing, login, signup) and authenticated layout with sidebar navigation\n2. **Landing page**: Hero section with product value prop, feature grid (6 cards), pricing teaser, and CTA\n3. **Login/Signup pages**: Form with email + password, error handling, redirect to dashboard on success\n4. **Protected layout**: Sidebar with navigation links (Dashboard, Incidents, Services, Schedules, Teams, Settings), top bar with user avatar and logout\n5. **Tailwind config**: Extended theme with OnCallShift brand colors (emerald-500 primary), dark mode by default\n6. **API client**: Axios instance with base URL from env, auth token interceptor, response error handling\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-28 17:47 UTC\n\n**Story 4: Frontend/backend integration** \u2014 completed by frontend_developer\n\nIntegrated the React frontend with Express backend:\n- Vite proxy config routes `/api/*` to backend on port 3001\n- Production Docker build serves frontend static files from Express\n- Health check page verifies backend connectivity\n- Environment variables: `VITE_API_URL`, `VITE_COGNITO_REGION`, `VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID`\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-28 18:03 UTC\n\n**Story 5: Production Dockerfile** \u2014 completed by devops_engineer\n\n**DEC-001: Multi-stage Docker build optimized for production**\n- Stage 1: Install dependencies with `npm ci --production=false`\n- Stage 2: Compile backend TypeScript to `dist/`\n- Stage 3: Build frontend with Vite to `frontend/dist/`\n- Stage 4: Production image with compiled backend + frontend static assets, Node 20 alpine (~180MB final image)\n- Express serves `frontend/dist/` as static files with `index.html` fallback for SPA routing\n- Health check: `HEALTHCHECK CMD curl -f http://localhost:3001/api/health || exit 1`\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-28 18:07 UTC\n\n**Story 6-8: Terraform infrastructure modules** \u2014 completed by devops_engineer\n\nCreated 3 Terraform modules for AWS infrastructure:\n\n1. **networking**: VPC with 2 public + 2 private subnets, NAT gateway, security groups for ALB \u2192 ECS \u2192 RDS\n2. **database**: RDS PostgreSQL 16, `db.t4g.micro`, automated backups (7 days), encrypted storage, private subnet placement\n3. **ecs-service**: ECS Fargate cluster, task definition (512 CPU / 1024 MB), ALB with health checks, auto-scaling (1-4 tasks), CloudWatch log group\n\nAll modules use variables for environment-specific config. Dev environment wired in `environments/dev/main.tf`.\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-30 12:04 UTC\n\n**Story 9-10: CI/CD pipelines** \u2014 completed by devops_engineer\n\n**DEC-001: GitHub Actions CI/CD with Terraform plan approval**\n\n1. **CI Workflow** (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`):\n   - Lint, typecheck, test for both backend and frontend\n   - Docker build verification\n   - `npm audit --audit-level=high`\n   - Triggered on push to main and PRs\n\n2. **Deploy Workflow** (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`):\n   - ECR push with `latest` and commit SHA tags\n   - ECS service update with force new deployment\n   - Smoke test against ALB health endpoint\n   - Manual trigger only (workflow_dispatch)\n\n3. **Terraform Workflow**: Plan on PR, apply on merge to main with issue-based approval\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-30 12:21 UTC\n\n**Story 11-12: Documentation and mobile scaffolding** \u2014 completed by backend_developer\n\nCreated comprehensive `CLAUDE.md` with:\n- Project structure and tech stack overview\n- Development commands (build, test, lint, deploy)\n- Database migration workflow\n- API route conventions and error handling patterns\n- Security requirements and forbidden patterns\n\nReact Native mobile app scaffolded with Expo:\n- Navigation structure (tab navigator + stack navigators)\n- Login screen with Cognito auth\n- Incident list screen (placeholder)\n- Push notification registration with Expo Push API\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-30 12:34 UTC\n\n\ud83d\udd04 Revision 1/3 requested by Tech Lead:\n\nThe monorepo structure is clean and well-organized. CI/CD pipelines follow best practices. Two issues: (1) Docker health check should use `wget` instead of `curl` since alpine doesn\'t include curl by default, (2) Terraform backend config should use S3 + DynamoDB for state locking instead of local state.\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-30 12:48 UTC\n\n**Revision fixes applied** \u2014 by devops_engineer\n\n1. \u2705 Changed Docker HEALTHCHECK to `wget --spider -q http://localhost:3001/api/health`\n2. \u2705 Added S3 backend config with DynamoDB state locking to Terraform\n3. \u2705 Added `backend.tf` with parameterized bucket and table names\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2025-12-30 12:52 UTC\n\n\u2705 PR approved by Tech Lead (score: 9/10)\n\nExcellent monorepo foundation. Clean separation of concerns across backend, frontend, mobile, and infrastructure. CI/CD pipelines are production-ready. The Terraform modules are well-structured with proper variable parameterization. Docker multi-stage build is efficient. Only minor deduction for the initial health check issue.\n\n\u2705 **All 12 stories completed** and approved by Tech Lead.\n\n\ud83d\udcdd **PR**: https://github.com/jarod-rosenthal/pagerduty-lite/pull/1\n\n*Ready for merge.*',
