      "# Infrastructure Deploy & Production Hardening\n\n> Dependencies: OCS-11 (integrations)\n\n## What This Ticket Delivers\n\nProduction deployment to AWS with Terraform, CloudFront CDN, SES email configuration, security hardening, and E2E test suite.\n\n## Infrastructure\n\n- **Compute**: ECS Fargate (1 API service + 5 background workers)\n- **Database**: RDS PostgreSQL 16 with automated backups\n- **CDN**: CloudFront serving frontend from S3\n- **Email**: SES with DKIM, MAIL FROM, and SPF for oncallshift.com\n- **Networking**: VPC with public/private subnets, NAT gateway, ALB\n\n## Security Hardening\n\n- Helmet security headers (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options)\n- Rate limiting on all endpoints\n- Input validation with Zod on all routes\n- API key hashing with bcrypt\n- Cloud credential encryption (AES-256-GCM)\n- Jira webhook HMAC verification\n\n## E2E Tests (Playwright)\n\n13 test files covering:\n- Authentication flow (login, signup, password reset)\n- Incident lifecycle (create, acknowledge, resolve)\n- Schedule management (create, add members, create override)\n- Service configuration (create, add integration)\n- Admin settings (update org, manage API keys)\n\n## Deploy Scripts\n\n- `deploy.sh`: Full deployment (ECR push + ECS update + CloudFront invalidation)\n- `deploy-backend.sh`: Backend-only deployment\n- Smoke tests verify health endpoint after deployment",
    buildLog:
      '**WorkerMill** \u2014 2026-01-07 14:00 UTC\n\n**Story 1-3: Terraform apply and ECS deployment** \u2014 completed by devops_engineer\n\n**DEC-001: Production infrastructure provisioned on AWS**\n\nApplied Terraform configuration to provision:\n\n1. **VPC**: 2 public subnets (us-east-1a, us-east-1b) + 2 private subnets. NAT gateway in public subnet for outbound internet from private subnet.\n2. **RDS PostgreSQL 16**: `db.t4g.micro` in private subnet. Automated backups (7-day retention), encrypted storage (aws/rds KMS key), multi-AZ disabled for cost (single-AZ dev).\n3. **ECS Cluster**: Fargate capacity provider. API service (512 CPU / 1024 MB, 1-4 tasks). 5 worker services (256 CPU / 512 MB each).\n4. **ALB**: HTTPS listener with ACM certificate for `oncallshift.com`. Health check against `/api/health` every 30 seconds.\n5. **CloudFront**: Distribution serving frontend from S3 origin. Custom domain `oncallshift.com` with ACM certificate. Cache policy: 1 hour for static assets, no-cache for API routes.\n6. **SES**: Domain verification for oncallshift.com. DKIM signing configured. MAIL FROM subdomain (mail.oncallshift.com) with SPF record.\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2026-01-07 14:25 UTC\n\n**Story 4-5: Deploy scripts and CI/CD** \u2014 completed by devops_engineer\n\n1. **deploy.sh** (9KB): Full deployment pipeline \u2014 Docker build \u2192 ECR push (with `latest` + commit SHA tags) \u2192 ECS service update (force new deployment) \u2192 Wait for stable \u2192 CloudFront invalidation \u2192 Smoke test.\n2. **deploy-backend.sh** (1.7KB): Backend-only deployment for API-only changes.\n3. **GitHub Actions workflows updated**: CI runs on all PRs. Deploy triggered on merge to main (changed to PR merge only, not direct push).\n4. **Smoke tests**: Post-deploy verification hits `/api/health`, checks response includes database connectivity, verifies CloudFront serves frontend.\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2026-01-07 14:40 UTC\n\n**Story 6-7: Security hardening** \u2014 completed by security_engineer\n\n**DEC-001: Security audit — all critical issues resolved**\n\n\u2705 **Headers**: Helmet configured with strict CSP (no inline scripts), HSTS (max-age 1 year, includeSubdomains), X-Frame-Options DENY, X-Content-Type-Options nosniff\n\u2705 **Rate limiting**: Global rate limit (100 req/min per IP). Endpoint-specific limits: auth routes (5/min), API key creation (3/hour), AI endpoints (10/min per user)\n\u2705 **Input validation**: Zod schemas on all 40 API routes. No raw `req.body` access anywhere.\n\u2705 **Secrets management**: API keys bcrypt-hashed (cost 12). Cloud credentials AES-256-GCM encrypted. No secrets in environment variable logs.\n\u2705 **CORS**: Allowed origins restricted to `oncallshift.com` and localhost for development.\n\u2705 **SQL injection**: TypeORM parameterized queries used exclusively. No raw SQL with string interpolation.\n\u2705 **Dependency audit**: `npm audit` shows 0 critical, 0 high vulnerabilities.\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2026-01-07 15:00 UTC\n\n**Story 8-9: E2E test suite** \u2014 completed by qa_engineer\n\n**DEC-001: Comprehensive E2E test coverage with Playwright**\n\nCreated 13 Playwright test files covering critical user flows:\n\n1. **Auth tests**: Login with valid/invalid credentials, signup flow, password reset, session persistence\n2. **Incident tests**: Create incident \u2192 verify in list \u2192 acknowledge \u2192 resolve \u2192 verify timeline\n3. **Schedule tests**: Create schedule \u2192 add layer \u2192 add members \u2192 verify on-call computation\n4. **Service tests**: Create service \u2192 add integration \u2192 verify integration key generated\n5. **Admin tests**: Update org settings \u2192 create API key \u2192 verify key works for auth\n6. **Mobile viewport tests**: Critical flows verified at 375x812 (iPhone) viewport\n\nTests use page objects pattern for maintainability. Fixtures provide seeded data (demo org, users, services).\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2026-01-07 15:15 UTC\n\n**Story 10: Production deploy verification** \u2014 completed by devops_engineer\n\nFinal deployment checklist:\n\n\u2705 `https://oncallshift.com` serves frontend (CloudFront \u2192 S3)\n\u2705 `https://oncallshift.com/api/health` returns 200 with database connectivity\n\u2705 Login flow works with Cognito\n\u2705 Incident creation \u2192 notification delivery \u2192 acknowledgment works end-to-end\n\u2705 SES email delivery verified (checked inbox for test notification)\n\u2705 SSL/TLS: A+ rating on SSL Labs\n\u2705 All 5 background workers running and processing queues\n\u2705 CloudWatch alarms configured and tested\n\n\u2705 PR approved by Tech Lead (score: 9/10)\n\nProduction infrastructure is solid. Security hardening covers all OWASP top 10. E2E tests provide good coverage of critical flows. The deploy scripts are well-structured with proper error handling.\n\n\u2705 **All 10 stories completed** and approved by Tech Lead.\n\n\ud83d\udcdd **PR**: https://github.com/jarod-rosenthal/pagerduty-lite/pull/22\n\n\ud83d\ude80 **Deployed to production at https://oncallshift.com**',
