      '**WorkerMill** \u2014 2026-01-27 16:44 UTC\n\n**Story 1-3: Backend refactoring (schedules, types, validation)** \u2014 completed by backend_developer\n\n**DEC-001: Service module decomposition for oversized route files**\n\n1. **OCS-789: Refactor schedules.ts** \u2014 Decomposed the 148KB monolith into focused service modules:\n   - `schedule-service.ts`: Core CRUD and rotation logic\n   - `schedule-layer-service.ts`: Layer management and stacking\n   - `schedule-override-service.ts`: Override CRUD with conflict detection\n   - `on-call-resolver.ts`: Who\'s-on-call computation engine\n   - Route file now only handles HTTP concerns (parsing, validation, response formatting)\n\n2. **OCS-792: Type-safe AI config route** \u2014 Defined `UserInterface`, `ApiRequestInterface` and replaced all `any` types in `ai-config.ts` with proper TypeScript interfaces.\n\n3. **OCS-794: Shared validation middleware** \u2014 Created `validateRequest(schema)` middleware that applies Zod validation to `req.body`, `req.params`, and `req.query`. Refactored all 40 route handlers to use the new middleware instead of inline validation.\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2026-01-27 17:15 UTC\n\n**Story 4-6: Frontend refactoring (components, colors, memory)** \u2014 completed by frontend_developer\n\n1. **OCS-783: Shared color utility** \u2014 Created `useColors()` hook with centralized color definitions. Refactored all mobile screens to use the hook instead of inline hex values. 3 stories (scaffold, refactor core screens, finalize remaining).\n\n2. **OCS-786: Incident detail decomposition** \u2014 Extracted from monolith into sub-components:\n   - `StepDisplay`: Escalation step visualization\n   - `OutputComponent`: Command output rendering\n   - `AutomationPanel`: Runbook automation controls\n   - `AIChatPanel`: AI diagnosis chat interface\n   Shared types extracted to `types/incident.ts`.\n\n3. **OCS-802: Memory leak fixes** \u2014 Identified and fixed memory leaks in 4 pages:\n   - Notification listener not cleaned up on unmount\n   - WebSocket connections not closed on page navigation\n   - Interval timers not cleared in dashboard polling\n   - Event listeners not removed in schedule calendar\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2026-01-29 00:38 UTC\n\n**Story 7-9: Security hardening** \u2014 completed by security_engineer\n\n1. **OCS-787: Jira webhook HMAC verification** \u2014 Re-enabled webhook signature verification that was temporarily disabled during development. Validates `x-hub-signature` header against shared secret using HMAC-SHA256.\n2. **Terraform secrets remediation** \u2014 Moved hardcoded database password from `terraform.tfvars` to AWS Secrets Manager. Updated ECS task definition to pull from Secrets Manager at runtime.\n3. **IAM policy scoping** \u2014 Replaced `Resource: "*"` with specific ARNs for SQS queues, SES identities, and S3 buckets. Applied principle of least privilege across all IAM roles.\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2026-01-29 14:57 UTC\n\n**Story 10-12: Testing and verification** \u2014 completed by qa_engineer\n\n1. **OCS-819: Jira webhook signature tests** \u2014 8 comprehensive tests: valid signature, invalid signature, missing header, expired timestamp, replay attack prevention, different HTTP methods.\n2. **OCS-824: Frontend sanitization** \u2014 XSS prevention audit across all components. Ensured all user-generated content renders through React\'s built-in escaping (no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`).\n3. **N+1 query verification** \u2014 Enabled TypeORM query logging, ran E2E tests, verified no N+1 patterns. The escalation timer fix (OCS-799) reduced schedule queries from O(n) to O(1) per tick.\n\n**WorkerMill** \u2014 2026-01-30 12:34 UTC\n\n**Story 13-15: Multi-provider AI and final cleanup** \u2014 completed by backend_developer\n\n1. **OCS-824: Multi-provider implementation** \u2014 Unified AI provider interface with runtime provider selection. Users can configure Anthropic Claude, OpenAI GPT-4, or Google Gemini per-organization. Provider-specific tool calling adapters handle the differences.\n2. **API client refactoring** \u2014 Consolidated 4 duplicated HTTP client implementations into a single `ApiClient` class with retry, timeout, and error handling.\n3. **Sign-out deduplication** \u2014 Fixed race condition where multiple sign-out requests could fire simultaneously. Promise-based deduplication ensures only one Cognito sign-out call.\n\n\u2705 PR approved by Tech Lead (score: 9/10)\n\nExcellent quality sprint. The schedules.ts decomposition from 148KB to focused service modules is a major maintainability win. Memory leak fixes and N+1 query elimination improve runtime stability. Security hardening with IAM scoping and webhook verification brings the codebase to production standards.\n\n\u2705 **All 15 stories completed** and approved by Tech Lead.\n\n\ud83d\udcdd **PR**: https://github.com/jarod-rosenthal/pagerduty-lite/pull/284\n\n*Ready for merge.*',
